<h2 id="iii-analysis-of-the-breakthroughs">III. Analysis of the Breakthroughs</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Policy focus</strong>: The 35 technologies were placed on the “open competition” list; special funds for integrated circuits, aero engines, and more have topped <strong>500 billion RMB</strong> cumulatively</li>
  <li><strong>Market pull</strong>: The world’s largest manufacturing base (30% of global output); annual sales of <strong>30 million</strong> new energy vehicles drive supply chain iteration</li>
  <li><strong>Corporate R&amp;D</strong>: Huawei, SMIC, and others invest over 100 billion RMB a year in R&amp;D; China’s R&amp;D intensity reached <strong>2.8%</strong> in 2024 (above the EU’s)</li>
  <li><strong>Industry-academia collaboration</strong>: The Chinese Academy of Sciences and enterprises have jointly built <strong>120</strong> joint laboratories</li>
</ul>

